  "configuration_id": "config_039",
  "reason": "Evidence: The top-3 results (config_021: 0.725, config_031: 0.721, config_045: 0.706) all use scvi_n200 + imagenet_vit_l + multiprofile, with transformer aggregation and weighted fusion being the best combination. The multiprofile space with these encoders is now well-mapped (both fusion types tested, both aggregation types tested). Key remaining uncertainty: whether the profile setting (multiprofile vs. singleprofile) is a meaningful design choice when paired with the best encoders. This experiment (config_039: singleprofile, scvi_n200, imagenet_vit_l, weighted) tests whether removing the multiprofile aggregation step degrades performance or whether the encoder quality alone is sufficient. If singleprofile is competitive, it offers a cheaper path (no aggregation) to similar accuracy; if it is clearly worse, it confirms multiprofile is essential and we can focus remaining budget on fine-tuning the multiprofile configuration. Expected cost: moderate-to-low (~2–3 GPU hours), since singleprofile eliminates the aggregation step while retaining the two encoder forward passes. With 3 experiments remaining after this one, resolving the profile-setting question now is the highest-value uncertainty reduction before final exploitation."
}

